/*
# Checkbox

A boolean control (docs/system-design/components-baseline.md, Contract 1). Its value is the
`checked` attribute; **`input` owns the value's destination** — by default the
destination is the checkbox itself, so it works standalone with zero wiring:

    mute: Checkbox [ label = "Mute" ]          … visible = { mute.checked }

Hand the value to its real owner by overriding `input` and constraining down:

    Checkbox [ label = "Mute", checked = { app.muted }, input(v: boolean) { app.muted = v } ]

`press()` never writes `checked` directly — it only delivers — so a bound checkbox
never fights its constraint.

```declare
row: View [ x = 20, y = 20,
    layout: SimpleLayout [ axis = y, spacing = 8 ],
    mute: Checkbox [ label = "Mute" ],
    Text [ text = { mute.checked ? "muted" : "audible" } ]
    ]
```

## checked
Whether the box is ticked. Standalone it owns this and you read it back by name; bound
(`checked = { app.muted }`) it needs an `input` override to go with it — **a one-way
binding with no `input` leaves the checkbox's own edit assigning to a constrained slot,
which is refused at runtime.**

## label
The text beside the box. `""` renders the box alone — the form for a checkbox inside a
table cell, where the column heading is the label.

## size
The box's edge length. Defaults to the theme's figure, so a toolbar checkbox can shrink
to match its neighbours without a subclass.

## input()
**Where the value goes.** The default writes `checked`; override it and the checkbox
becomes a delivery channel for state you own (`input(v: boolean) { app.muted = v }`).
This is the one member to override when the value lives elsewhere.

## press()
Toggles by delivering the flipped value through `input` — **never by writing `checked`**,
which is what keeps a bound checkbox from fighting its constraint. Called by a click and
by Space/Enter.

## focusShape()
Rings the box alone, not the box-plus-label — the Radio rule, so a long label does not
drag a wide ring across the row.

## onClick
Runs `press()` when enabled. Override `input` instead if what you want is the value.
*/

include [ "control.declare" ]

class Checkbox extends Control [

    // keyboard focus rings the BOX alone, not box+label (the Radio rule)

    focusShape() { return ({ x: this.box.x, y: this.box.y, w: this.box.width, h: this.box.height, rad: this.box.cornerRadius }) },
    height = 24,
    checked: boolean = false,
    label:   string = "",

    // the box's size: the theme fact by default, one attribute to override
    // (a toolbar checkbox can shrink to its neighbors without a subclass)

    size: number = 0,             // 0 = theme.checkboxSize (else 20)

    input(v: boolean) { checked = v },

    press()   { input(!checked) },
    onClick() { if (!disabled) press() },

    width   = { this.box.width + (label == "" ? 0 : 8 + this.cap.width) },
    opacity = { disabled ? (typeof theme.disabledOpacity == "number" ? theme.disabledOpacity : 0.45) : 1 },

    box: View [ y = { (parent.height - this.height) / 2 },
        width  = { classroot.size > 0 ? classroot.size : typeof theme.checkboxSize == "number" ? theme.checkboxSize : 20 },
        height = { this.width },
        cornerRadius = { typeof theme.checkboxRadius == "number" ? theme.checkboxRadius : Math.min(8, Math.max(3, theme.controlRadius - 2)) },
        fill   = { checked ? theme.accent : theme.control },
        stroke = { stroke(1, checked ? theme.accent : hot || down ? theme.textMuted : theme.line) },

        // the mark is DRAWN (reactive draw(), not a glyph): pixel-identical on
        // both backends, independent of any font

        // The tick, from the shared set. This was drawn here at stroke 2.5
        // with mitered joins while the menu drew the same tick at 1.8 with
        // round ones — one shape, two hands. Sized from the BOX, which is a
        // theme fact (14 in Cupertino, 20 in Redmond), so `iconSize` is
        // overridden here rather than inherited: the prevailing value is a
        // default, not a rule.

        mark: CheckIcon [ visible = { checked },
            iconSize = { parent.width * 0.72 },
            x = { (parent.width - this.width) / 2 }, y = { (parent.height - this.height) / 2 },
            ink = { theme.accentText } ]
        ],

    // the label rides the BOX, not a constant: its gap is box-relative (the
    // box's size is a theme fact — 14 in Cupertino, 20 in Redmond), and both
    // center in the control's height, so they align automatically everywhere

    // NO explicit textColor: the label follows the PREVAILING text style
    // (the App's default is theme.text, so nothing changes anywhere) — and a
    // use site restyles it with ordinary attributes, no subclass:
    //     Checkbox [ label = "Grouped", fontSize = 12.5, textColor = { theme.textMuted }, size = 16 ]

    cap: Text [ x = { parent.box.width + 8 }, y = center, wrap = false,
        visible = { label != "" }, text = { label } ]
    ]
